A hosted execution adapter implements Agent's public methods and state, not
its private fields. AgentSession already accepts that object at runtime;
make its type structural and expose a version for fail-closed host startup.
createAgentSession builds the Agent itself, from options that carry pi's
request settings, provider hooks, cache warming and context transform, so a
host that rebuilt the session by hand would drift from pi. Let a host build
the agent from those same options instead.

A hosted agent can also queue words itself, as a conversation reopens and
the host carries on a turn a restart cut off. pi's screen draws its pending
list from the session's own queue, which only steer, followUp and prompt
fill, and each of those runs the extensions' input handlers again and
queues the words on the agent a second time. showQueued puts words the
agent already holds on that list, so they show as pending as pi's own do;
pi takes them off as their message starts or on clearQueue, as it does its
own. Nothing in pi calls it, so a pi no host drives behaves as before.

Offered upstream as the structural AgentSession execution seam. Apply only
to the host's private pi build; ordinary interactive pi stays unchanged.

